      "title": "Clinical Research Funding Officer (Part-Time, Term)",
      "description": "Clinical Research Funding Officer (Part-Time, Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Clinical Research Funding Officer (Part-Time, Term) Date Posted: 08/31/2026 Req ID: 50022 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Dentistry Department: Faculty of Dentistry Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059992 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Exciting new advances and global challenges are radically reshaping the field of dentistry. Our vision at the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto is to not just address and respond to these changes – but to thoughtfully and conscientiously shape the field of the future. With our robust and comprehensive educational training programs (DDS, MSc, PhD degrees, IDAPP and other specialty programs), our emphasis on community outreach and care, and our internationally known and interdisciplinary research mission, the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto continues to earn its reputation as one of the top dental schools in North America. Throughout more than 150 years of dental education -- the oldest, largest and most comprehensive training program in Canada -- we have striven to graduate the highest quality of students while providing the public the highest standards of care. We are driving by our vision to improve health by advancing dentistry through inspired leadership, innovation, and excellence in education, research and practice. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Vice-Dean, Research you will play a key role in advising faculty on clinical funding application strategies, coordinating and guiding applicants through the various phases of clinical research funding application process. You will provide detailed information to faculty on completing, submitting, and coordinating clinical research applications. Your role includes advising on improvements to draft funding proposals to better meet requirements, conducting analysis on research trends, and keeping well-informed on research funding programs, application guidelines, policies/procedures and regulations funding. You will play an integral role in researching and recommending new opportunities for external funding. Please note this is for a part-time (50% FTE) term position with a duration of 22-months. Your responsibilities will include: Advising faculty on clinical funding application strategies Providing detailed information to faculty on completing, submitting, and coordinating research applications Researching, analyzing and recommending solutions to research funding applications issues Coordinating the preparation of submission materials Keeping well-informed on clinical and industry-sponsored funding opportunities and resources, application policies/procedures and key deadlines Liaising with academic units and stakeholders to support research funding initiatives Acting as a liaison between patients and Dentistry’s clinical researchers, as required Monitoring department budget to ensure expenditures remain within budgeted allocations Serving as a resource to others by providing (non-supervisory) guidance related to grant research funding, as appropriate Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three years of recent related experience in research administration, including managing grant proposal processes, preferably in a health-related, clinical, or multi-disciplinary research institution. Demonstrated experience and a successful track record of researching and sourcing relevant funding opportunities, and developing and implementing plans to attain such funding opportunities. Demonstrated experience with tailoring and editing grant proposals in alignment with the selection/evaluation criteria of the research funding program. Strong interpersonal skillsdemonstrated through building relationships with relevant stakeholders. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong computer skills (Excel, Access, Word, PowerPoint). Strong project management, organizational and time management skills to manage multiple competing priorities.High degree of initiative. Sound decision making, analytical and problem solving skills and an attention to detail. Strong client services orientation and relationship management skills To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Proactive Resourceful Self-directed Team player Please note this is for a part-time (50% FTE) term position with a duration of 22-months.. Closing Date: 09/13/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Part-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 11 -- $38,288 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $48,964. Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Clinical Research, Medical Research, Relationship Manager, Clinic, Part Time, Healthcare, Customer Service Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
