      "description": "Executive Assistant to AVP, Institutional Strategy & Director of Operations, President's Office Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Executive Assistant to AVP, Institutional Strategy & Director of Operations, President's Office Date Posted: 08/28/2026 Req ID: 50020 Faculty/Division: Office of the President Department: Office of the President Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Position Summary: Reporting to the Office Manager & Executive Assistant to the President, the Executive Assistant to the AVP, Institutional Strategy and Director of Operations, Office of the President (Executive Assistant) supports the Office Manager & Executive Assistant to the President in preparing and managing the President’s schedule and serves as the primary scheduling and administrative support to the Assistant Vice-President, Institutional Strategies and the Director of Operations. This includes managing complex calendars; coordinating meetings and high-level engagements; booking travel; identifying and prioritizing urgent or sensitive issues; preparing executive briefings and background materials; independently drafting complex and confidential correspondence; and ensuring Senior Leadership are informed of key decisions, operational issues, and emerging matters. The role requires strong administrative skills and sound judgment in resolving inquiries independently and redirecting issues as appropriate. The Executive Assistant serves as the designated back-up to both the Executive Assistant to the President and reception and correspondence units, ensuring continuity of executive support and day-to-day office operations during absences and peak workload periods. The incumbent will have daily access to confidential and sensitive information related to all areas of the University’s functioning including financial, budgetary, and human resources information.  The incumbent works in a complex environment that requires a high degree of sensitivity, responsiveness and a need to maintain absolute confidentiality. The incumbent must present a professional image in the Office of the President by interacting knowledgeably and courteously with the many people including governors, senior administrators, faculty, staff, students and community members who come into contact with the Office of the President. Qualifications Required: Education: University degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: Six to Eight (6-8) years of experience supporting senior executive(s), preferably within a post-secondary or government environment. Experience drafting correspondence, preparing briefing packages and presentations, organizing and coordinating special events. Demonstrated experience in liaising with senior administrators, responding to and handling matters of a complex, confidential and sensitive nature. Experience with organizing complex meeting schedules. Knowledge about protocol, diplomacy and an excellent understanding of the University’s mission and intersection with the broader community Skills: Demonstrated superior writing and editing skills. Superior communications skills, both written and verbal (e.g., drafting written correspondence, minutes, proposals). Advanced computer skills in Microsoft Office (must be able to set up templates and macros in Word and Excel, set up Excel spreadsheets and graphics, and prepare sophisticated PowerPoint presentations), and scheduling software. Familiarity with Microsoft SharePoint and TEAMS an asset. Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills. Experience with Concur or other expense systems. Other: Proven effectiveness relating to all levels of the University – administration, faculty, staff, students, and external members of the community. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Ability to set priorities, manage multiple tasks and projects and meet deadlines. Proven track record of using good judgment in dealing with issues in a fast-paced, dynamic environment. Excellent interpersonal skills: ability to work collaboratively and positively in a team setting. Thoroughness and careful attention to detail. Tact, discretion, sensitivity to confidential matters. Ability to organize a heavy and fluctuating workload in a changing environment. Ability to assimilate and interpret significant amounts of information. Ability to work effectively and professionally, both independently and within a team environment. Ability to analyze information and prepare documents within the parameters set by the Senior Leaders. Demonstrated ability to track, manage and compile information and data. NOTE: Please submit your résumé along with a customized one-page cover letter. Closing Date: 09/10/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 1 -- Hiring Zone: $76,641 - $89,415 -- Broadband Salary Range: $76,641 - $127,734 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Event Planning, Operations Manager, Secretary, Sharepoint, Developer, Hospitality, Operations, Administrative, Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant-Associate-or-Full-Professor-Academic-Movement-Disorders-Neurologist-ON/604769517/": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate or Full Professor",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate or Full Professor - Academic Movement Disorders Neurologist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant / Associate or Full Professor - Academic Movement Disorders Neurologist Date Posted: 07/28/2026 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 49514 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Medicine Hospital Affiliation: University Health Network (UHN) & Sinai Health System (SHS) Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Division of Neurology, Department of Medicine, University Health Network/Sinai Health System (UHN/SHS) and the Temerty Faculty of Medicine, University of Toronto is seeking a full-time, permanent Academic Neurologist with a focus on movement disorders. The candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or higher with a preference of the position description of Clinician Investigator at the University of Toronto. The effective start date is at a mutually agreed upon date after January 1, 2027. Academic appointment will be within the Division of Neurology, Department of Medicine, University of Toronto and teaching will be as per Division of Neurology requirements. Research and clinical focus will be on movement disorders and clinical service will be in the Division of Neurology, Krembil Brain Institute for on-call, inpatient and ambulatory care. The successful candidate will hold a MD degree or equivalent and should have, or be eligible for, certification in Neurology by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada and licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario (CPSO). To be considered for the Clinician Investigator position, specific additional training such as a Master’s degree or equivalent is required and scholarly excellence as demonstrated by the presence of research grants, publications in leading journals, invited presentations at significant conferences, awards, accolades, and other related accomplishments. Salary will be commensurate with training and experience and in the range of $290,000-295,000 CAD per year dependent on clinical work. Applications will be accepted until September 30, 2026 . Please send your curriculum vitae, three references letters and a letter of application to: Dr. Hans Katzberg, Division of Neurology, Toronto General Hospital 200 Elizabeth Street, Toronto ON, Canada M5G 2C4. Email: hans.katzberg@uhn.ca CAUTION: This ad is “posted only” to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. For more information about the Department of Medicine, University of Toronto visit https://www.deptmedicine.utoronto.ca . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Neurology, Academic, Physician, CAD, Healthcare, Education, Engineering, Research Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
